    {
      "id": 143291,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-06-28T13:53:53.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>From Spiff's Sentinel Tactics FAQ:</p><p><span>Ambuscade will trigger his own traps if he enters a hex with a trap marker (because he’s a target moving into the trap’s hex), and the explosion could hurt his allies if they are within range of the explosion, but as mentioned in the “who’s making the attack?” section of this FAQ, since the traps don’t have hp, their attack is actually being made by ambuscade himself and characters are immune to their own attacks, so the traps cannot damage ambuscade. https://greaterthangames.com/comment/81702#comment-81702</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, I didn't see it in the FAQ, but I recall the ruling on Automated Hunter being that since Automated Hunter is _NOT_ a separate target, Ambuscade can not be hurt by its attack.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:20:41.617Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 13203,
      "topic_slug": "quick-question-or-beginners-questions",
      "display_username": "arenson9",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>From Spiff&#39;s Sentinel Tactics FAQ:</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Ambuscade will trigger his own traps if he enters a hex with a trap marker (because he&rsquo;s a target moving into the trap&rsquo;s hex), and the explosion could hurt his allies if they are within range of the explosion, but as mentioned in the &ldquo;who&rsquo;s making the attack?&rdquo; section of this FAQ, since the traps don&rsquo;t have hp, their attack is actually being made by ambuscade himself and characters are immune to their own attacks, so the traps cannot damage ambuscade. https://greaterthangames.com/comment/81702#comment-81702</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, I didn&#39;t see it in the FAQ, but I recall the ruling on Automated Hunter being that since Automated Hunter is _NOT_ a separate target, Ambuscade can not be hurt by its attack.&nbsp;</p>",
