    {
      "id": 143296,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-06-30T03:45:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Phantom5613\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/48/1906_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Phantom5613:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's for the help, everyone!More questions I have:With melee attacks against Omnitron(who is always one elevation higher) I'm guessing rolls of 1 never hit?Since they are his own attacks, Ambuscade can 'Aim' his explosives, correct?&nbsp; and since he can only aim one attack, it would have to be against one selective target for each 'Aim' I use, right?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If you are on elevation two and attacking a hex that Omnitron is on that is elevation one, then your effective range is only one.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Yes, Ambuscade can aim his explosives, and yes an aimed attack only ever applies the effect of the aim against the first target that defends that attack.</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:20:41.966Z",
